{title: Waltzing Matilda}
{artist: Banjo Paterson}
{level: Easy}
{duration: 3.0}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 108}
{strum: dduudu-4-4}

{start_of_grid: Verse}
| C | G7 | C | G7 | C | F | C | G7 | C |
{end_of_grid}

{start_of_grid: Chorus}
| C | G7 | C | G7 | C | F | C | G7 | C |
{end_of_grid}

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]Once a jolly swagman camped by a [G7]billabong
[C]Under the shade of a [G7]coolibah tree
[C]And he sang as he watched and waited till his [F]billy boiled
[C]"You'll come a-[G7]waltzing Matilda with [C]me"

{comment: Chorus}
[C]Waltzing Matilda, [G7]waltzing Matilda
[C]You'll come a-[G7]waltzing Matilda with me
[C]And he sang as he watched and waited till his [F]billy boiled
[C]"You'll come a-[G7]waltzing Matilda with [C]me"

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]Down came a jumbuck to drink at that [G7]billabong
[C]Up jumped the swagman and [G7]grabbed him with glee
[C]And he sang as he shoved that jumbuck in his [F]tucker bag
[C]"You'll come a-[G7]waltzing Matilda with [C]me"

{comment: Verse 3}
[C]Up rode the squatter, mounted on his [G7]thoroughbred
[C]Down came the troopers, [G7]one, two, three
[C]"Where's that jolly jumbuck you've got in your [F]tucker bag?"
[C]"You'll come a-[G7]waltzing Matilda with [C]me"
